## PHASE 5: Security & Backend Hardening (Section 13)

### 5A. Server-Side Data Protection

Audit these files:
- backend/routes/tracking.ts — phone/email/address never sent to unauthenticated
- backend/routes/donor.ts — donor contact info protected
- backend/middleware/auth.ts — authorization on all protected endpoints
- backend/routes/admin.ts — admin-only data stays admin-only

### 5B. Input Validation

- Verify all routes validate input (Zod schemas in backend/validation/)
- Client AND server validation for: WhatsApp (10 digits), phone, pincode, blood group

---

## PHASE 6: Testing & Verification

### 6A. Update Test Environment
- setup-env.ts — Supabase stubs removed (Phase 1E)
- All test files — VITE_SUPABASE_URL removed (Phase 1E)
- Verify tests pass with TEST_MODE flag only

### 6B. Run Full Test Suite
```
npm run test:all
```

### 6C. Manual Verification Checklist

- New donor → profile popup → complete profile → dashboard
- Existing donor → dashboard → update availability
- Donor WhatsApp → exactly 10 digits → save
- Requester → simple registration → create request
- Requester → broadcast → compatible donors notified
- Donor → receives request → accepts/responds
- Requester → sees donor response → tracks request
- Public request page → safe info visible → protected locked
- New user → tries to unlock → sign up required
- Institution → select type → register → pending approval
- Admin → review institution → approve/reject/suspend
- Approved institution → dashboard → inventory/donors/requests
- Admin → complete platform data visible
- Google login → FindMyDonor flow → correct redirect
- Track code → valid code returns correct request
- Invalid tracking code → clear error
- Donor availability → real counts update
- Mobile and desktop → no broken layout

### 6D. Lint & Type Check
```
npm run lint
```

